142
01:24:01,926 --> 01:24:14,291
[SPEAKER_14]: Honors Pilot for Career Technical Education, CTE, at Medford High School, presented by Dr. Kim Talbot, Assistant Superintendent for Academics and Instruction, and Mr. Chad Fallon, Executive Director of CTE.

143
01:24:15,332 --> 01:24:15,652
[SPEAKER_14]: Welcome.

144
01:24:28,252 --> 01:24:28,672
[SPEAKER_01]: Good evening.

145
01:24:33,735 --> 01:24:39,218
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm really pleased to be here tonight to share another exciting step forward for career and technical education at Medford High School.

146
01:24:39,959 --> 01:24:43,341
[SPEAKER_01]: I want to first recognize how much our CTE programming continues to grow.

147
01:24:44,061 --> 01:24:53,627
[SPEAKER_01]: With the recent Chapter 74 approval of plumbing and information support services and networking, we now offer 17 state-approved CTE programs at Medford High.

148
01:24:54,664 --> 01:24:59,485
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's something I'm extremely proud of, and it means more opportunities and more pathways for our students.

149
01:25:00,426 --> 01:25:04,067
[SPEAKER_01]: You'll also hear us using the word major much more intentionally this year.

150
01:25:04,987 --> 01:25:08,628
[SPEAKER_01]: Each of these 17 CTE programs represents a student's major.

151
01:25:09,148 --> 01:25:11,689
[SPEAKER_01]: They aren't electives or simply classes students take.

152
01:25:12,489 --> 01:25:25,035
[SPEAKER_01]: Our students spend approximately 50% of their high school experience in their CTE major developing technical skills, completing rigorous coursework, earning industry credentials, and gaining real-world experience.

153
01:25:26,396 --> 01:25:32,059
[SPEAKER_01]: As these programs continue to grow, I think it's equally important that we continue to recognize the rigor and achievement within them.

154
01:25:33,223 --> 01:25:41,650
[SPEAKER_01]: That brings us to what I'm really excited to share tonight, our new career tech education honors pilot for the 2026-27 school year.

155
01:25:42,731 --> 01:25:48,135
[SPEAKER_01]: We're beginning with engineering, health assisting, film and television production, and programming and web development.

156
01:25:49,176 --> 01:26:00,104
[SPEAKER_01]: Honors will be optional, earned, and performance-based, with students demonstrating that higher level of achievement through either cooperative education or a rigorous capstone experience.

157
01:26:01,070 --> 01:26:06,353
[SPEAKER_01]: We're also continuing to look for ways to strengthen the academic experiences connected to all of our CTE majors.

158
01:26:06,854 --> 01:26:18,241
[SPEAKER_01]: One example this year is the addition of Design 1 for our Graphic Design and Visual Communication students, which gives them a stronger foundation in the principles of design and complements the technical work they're already doing.

159
01:26:19,568 --> 01:26:30,876
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm really proud of the direction we're moving in, and as our CTE programs continue to grow, we want our students to see their CTE major as a rigorous, challenging, and important part of their future.

160
01:26:31,736 --> 01:26:37,900
[SPEAKER_01]: Whether that future is college, career, apprenticeship, union, or further training, we support our students.

161
01:26:38,681 --> 01:26:42,864
[SPEAKER_01]: So with that, I'd like to walk you through the honors pilot and what we hope to accomplish this year.

162
01:26:44,085 --> 01:26:48,968
[SPEAKER_01]: And I do just want to say a special thank you to Dr. Talbot for her support and guidance through this project.

163
01:26:56,494 --> 01:27:07,519
[SPEAKER_01]: So the vision for CTE is to be a defining part of the Medford High School experience, where students discover their strengths, develop real-world skills, and prepare for successful futures.

164
01:27:08,560 --> 01:27:16,684
[SPEAKER_01]: A student's CTE program is their major, a rigorous pathway that combines academics, hands-on learning, credentials, and real-world experiences.

165
01:27:17,595 --> 01:27:23,417
[SPEAKER_01]: Whether the next step is college, career, apprenticeship, union, military, or further training, our goal is simple.

166
01:27:24,077 --> 01:27:28,878
[SPEAKER_01]: Every CTE student graduates with skills, options, and a plan for what comes next.

167
01:27:28,898 --> 01:27:31,119
