168
01:27:31,139 --> 01:27:31,259
[SPEAKER_01]: OK.

169
01:27:33,399 --> 01:27:46,003
[SPEAKER_01]: Per the Department of Education guidance, Chapter 74 cooperative education and approved post-secondary articulation are considered advanced coursework, comparable to AP, IB, and dual enrollment.

170
01:27:47,237 --> 01:27:57,927
[SPEAKER_01]: So in Medford, students who successfully complete a cooperative education experience are already meeting this high bar and are reported to the state and completed advanced coursework.

171
01:27:59,789 --> 01:28:06,194
[SPEAKER_01]: But through the years, for a variety of reasons, not all students who have the prerequisite skills to engage in co-op are able to do so.

172
01:28:07,195 --> 01:28:11,900
[SPEAKER_01]: So despite this reporting structure, the grades students earn are assigned a standard weighting.

173
01:28:16,995 --> 01:28:25,262
[SPEAKER_01]: The challenge is that CTE students, as you probably know, spend approximately 50% of their school day in technical instruction.

174
01:28:26,323 --> 01:28:32,588
[SPEAKER_01]: Advanced coursework currently receives standard GPA weighting, so all of our programs now receive standard weighting.

175
01:28:33,569 --> 01:28:41,075
